WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.340
I just got back to my hotel room and my phone&nbsp;
is in need of a charge. What are my options?&nbsp;

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:13.080
Okay, here are three options: one is I take this&nbsp;
USB cable, plug into the slot in the clock radio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:18.180
and then charge my phone from that. What could&nbsp;
possibly go wrong? I'll tell you what could go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:24.060
wrong, is that this device could have been&nbsp;
tampered with, and it will now use the data&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.160
transfer capabilities of this cable to either&nbsp;
plant malware on my device or take sensitive data&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:34.800
off of it. I don't want to do that! That's known as&nbsp;
a "juice jacking" attack. I could use a specially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.200
made adapter like this that disables the data&nbsp;
transfer and only allows transfer of pure power.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:47.280
Or the traditional option-- the wall charger right&nbsp;
here into the AC outlet. And I'm probably going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.260
to get a faster charge, I'm going to avoid the&nbsp;
juice jacking scenario, and I'm going to be safer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.780
After all, you don't know where this thing's been!&nbsp;
Don't just go plugging this in anywhere. Be safe!

